nwang@black.clarku.edu (Clueless newbie) writes:
>Could someone post a general rule for wishing an item.  This time I
>bought an lamp and rubbed it, something popped up and granted me a wish.
>I read an post that Stormbringer is a pretty good weapon, so I typed "A
>blessed broadsword named Stormbringer" or something, and it just keep on
>saying no such thing in the game, eventually I got a spell book, and an
>orc came in took my head off :(
>
>So if anyone knows the syntax rules for wishing, please post it or mail
>it to me, thanks!

It would have worked if you hadn't typed "A."  I believe the syntax is

[count] [blessed_state] [enchantment] [item] [named <artifactname>]

(count, blessed_state, enchantment, and artifact name are all optional and
only apply when it makes sense (to the game)... (3 scrolls, not 3 broadswords;
long sword named Excalibur, not amulet named Excalibur...)

For example, "blessed +3 war hammer named Mjollnir" or
             "3 blessed potions of gain ability"

